Package: scaleL
Title: Bayesian Imputation of Likert Scale Length for Meta-Analysis
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("scaleL", "Authors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "scaleL.pkg@proton.me")
Description: Bayesian imputation of missing Likert scale length L in
    meta-analytic data sets. Combines a variance-bound likelihood -- with
    three methods (empirical Monte-Carlo reference histograms (default),
    full 2-D quadrature, and a fast profile feasibility screen) -- with a
    structured prior over L (generic, corpus-empirical, field-specific,
    instrument-specific, or user-supplied) to produce per-study posteriors,
    multiple imputations, and pooled random-effects estimates via Rubin's
    rules. Also imputes a missing scale origin jointly with L, imputes
    missing standard deviations on bounded scales (single and multiple
    imputation), and provides an across-study-means channel for a second
    likelihood over L. Designed as a lightweight drop-in for downstream
    meta-analysis workflows.
